  <!-- LOCAL KNOWLEDGE SECTION -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">WOOLTON LOCAL KNOWLEDGE</span>
      <h2>Why Woolton Needs a Plumber Who Knows L25</h2>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <p>Woolton is one of Liverpool's most affluent suburbs. The L25 average house price is around £401,000. Beaconsfield Road plots have sold for over £10,000 per square foot. The top end runs £1.5 million to £2.4 million.</p>

        <p>That matters when something leaks. A burst pipe in a Quarry Street home can wreck original cornicing, period floorboards and top-end finishes in minutes. The cost to put it right is high. Speed and the right fault call save real money.</p>

        <p>The Woolton Conservation Area also limits what you can do outside the home. New flues, satellite dishes, condensate runs and any visible changes to listed homes need council approval. We've worked in the heritage streets for years. We plan jobs to avoid council headaches.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <p>Most Woolton homes are owned, not rented. People here tend to stay put. The plumbing has been changed and added to many times across each home's life. Original pipework runs alongside 1970s add-ons and modern combi swaps.</p>

        <p>Finding a leak in a 5-bed home with three bathrooms and decades of changes takes skill. Water shows up in one place. It often starts somewhere else. We carry heat-camera kit and acoustic leak gear to find the source before opening any walls.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- COMMON JOBS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
