        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does an emergency plumber cost in Woolton?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>£80 an hour weekdays 9am to 5pm. £120 an hour weekends 9am to 1pm. £150 an hour out of hours, nights and bank holidays. 1 hour minimum on every call-out. Parts at cost. Most jobs cost £80 to £350 total. Written quote before work starts. No separate call-out fee.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">RESPONSE</span>&nbsp; How quickly can you reach Woolton?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>30 minute response across Woolton L25. We dispatch from Kirkby. Typical arrival is 25 to 30 minutes via the M62 and M57. A real person answers the phone any time of day or night.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">LISTED</span>&nbsp; Do you work on Woolton's listed buildings?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. The Woolton heritage zone covers a large part of the village. Many homes on Beaconsfield Road, Quarry Street and Church Road are listed or in the protected streets. We plan work around original features. For listed buildings we give you the paperwork you need for listed building consent.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">LEAKS</span>&nbsp; Can you find a hidden leak without opening walls?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes, in most cases. We carry heat-camera kit that spots temperature differences behind walls and under floors. This pinpoints the source of a hidden leak before any plaster is opened. We always try non-invasive leak finding first. Call 0151 558 0334 for a same-day check.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">DETACHED</span>&nbsp; Do you cover larger detached homes with multi-zone heating?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. The detached homes on Hillside Drive, Baroncroft Road and the wider Woolton area often have two or three heating zones, mains pressure cylinders feeding several bathrooms, and top-brand fittings. We're G3 trained for unvented work and know Hansgrohe, Grohe, Villeroy & Boch and the other big brands.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">RETIREMENT</span>&nbsp; Do you cover Reynolds Court and other retirement properties?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Reynolds Court on Vale Road and the wider retirement housing in Woolton are familiar work. We work with managing agents for access to shared areas. We explain faults clearly without jargon and agree the price up front before any work begins.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are your engineers Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. All gas work is done by our own Gas Safe engineers. Check our entry at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. It's against the law to work on gas without it.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">GUARANTEE</span>&nbsp; Do you guarantee your work?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Every job carries a 12-month workmanship guarantee. If something we fixed fails because of our work, we come back. No charge.</p></div></details>
